d like to share a note\n\nPedini wrote: Hey guys, thanks so much for the questions, they are great. At the moment, it is obvious that EU is in a trading range, and there have been some fake moves on either side and trapping people trading the range. I would personally choose to stay out till it resolves itself.\n\nAs for your questions, what I will do when I see an engulf is ask myself \"does this engulf make sense?\" By that I mean look at the\n\n2144\n\nhistory around where price engulfed. Did it engulf into a DP or a key level? Did it engulf into supply/demand. Also, look where the source of the engulf came from, was it coming from a HTF supply/demand level or has it failed yet to reach one? All these things should give you a heads up on a potential FO.\n\nFor example, if price is engulfing south, but price has yet to come off a significant level of supply, it makes sense to see a FO to help push price to higher levels. Something that looks like it may be currently happening on EU.\n\nAnyway, I hope this gives some food for thought, it is past 2am, so excuse my lack of a detailed information/charts, I will try to find some example to post when I am well rested.\n\nPeds\n\nPoints being: - An engulf must happen first and make sense (i.e. price engulfs a DP or keylevel, or \"into\" S/D) next: - The source of engulf. FO often happens when the source of engulf failed to reach the right zone (i.e. HTF S/D)\n\nLogic: engulf first, then FO. I haven't seen any engulf that comes after FO.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#19","p":1,"im":[],"m":19},{"id":"fakeouts_p1_22","t":"Two historical places will be analyzed here (marked by red circles below). Place for analysis 1 represents the history for the FL. And place for analysis 2 represents the history for one of 1W highs that we are focusing on - the S/R flip in 1d and 1w.","a":"Tj","d":"","n":"#22","p":1,"im":["3153a059e0e243ca000e7c639c7711cf3d32bf39","8b9d730fcfe665be1b5ff54309c6196e1785c426"],"m":22},{"id":"fakeouts_p1_23","t":"Clo